0..55 Comment "//! Completion handles an overlap that parts at a call."
56..59 Comment "//!"
60..135 Comment "//! The two `swap` rules overlap at `swap(Zero, n)`. One reduct is `n`. The"
136..171 Comment "//! other reduct is `add(n, Zero)`."
172..175 Comment "//!"
176..250 Comment "//! Completion derives a rule from `add(n, Zero)` to `n`. The derived rule"
251..324 Comment "//! follows from the written rules, because both sides are reducts of one"
325..400 Comment "//! peak. The derived rule joins the pair, and completion decides the pairs"
401..480 Comment "//! again (§ 7 of the cited work). The kernel reads it with the written rules."
481..484 Comment "//!"
485..500 Comment "//! - see: #338"
501..566 Comment "//! - cites: [Knuth-1970-simple_word_problems_universal_algebras]"
567..570 Comment "//!"
571..742 Comment "//! [Knuth-1970-simple_word_problems_universal_algebras]: https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-0-08-012975-4.50028-X \"Knuth and Bendix, Simple Word Problems in Universal Algebras\""
744..817 Comment "/// The naturals with addition and an operation whose two rules part at a"
818..827 Comment "/// call."
